00:48:33.620 --> 00:48:39.360
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: Your Honor, the threshold is suspicious or suspicion or suspicious circumstances, Your Honor.

00:48:40.960 --> 00:49:10.690
AMLC Executive Director Atty. Ronel U. Buenaventura: So that I cannot say whether it's conclusive or not but on the end of the covered person it's for them to determine based on the profile of their client based on the nature of the transaction whether this transaction is or activity is suspicious or not whether if on their end it is conclusive or not it's for them the threshold at least insofar as the law requires is suspicion or suspicious but if they are It could be that on their end, they have conclusively determined, but we have no personal knowledge on that, Your Honor.

00:49:11.170 --> 00:49:28.980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: With your indulgence, Atty. Mark, what do the guidelines or the law say when it made mention of the word require? When in doubt, should banks report? Or when in doubt, banks will not?

