Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Objection, Your Honor. It's both speculative and vague. There are too much possible answers to that, Your Honor. Perhaps the good counsel can be more specific, Your Honor.

07:04:44.410 --> 07:04:44.930
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: If

07:04:44.930 --> 07:04:47.650
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: the witness knows, counsel.

07:04:47.650 --> 07:04:48.450
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Submitted, Your Honor.

07:04:48.450 --> 07:04:52.390
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Ma'am Raquel, alam niyo ba yung sagot sa katanungan niya?

07:04:52.970 --> 07:04:53.890
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes, sir.

07:04:53.890 --> 07:04:54.570
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly answer.

07:04:56.460 --> 07:04:59.360
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: These are two different or distinct individuals, sir.

07:04:59.520 --> 07:05:00.320
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Correct.

07:05:03.520 --> 07:05:17.440
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: You identified the account with number 0161-4627-30, correct?

07:05:18.930 --> 07:05:21.510
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes, sir. That's the account of attorney Carpio, sir.

07:05:21.690 --> 07:05:22.030
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Correct.

07:05:25.170 --> 07:05:33.270
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: And your bank, the LVP, maintains account information for each individual account holder. Correct?

07:05:33.510 --> 07:05:34.030
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:05:35.330 --> 07:05:41.970
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Statements and account notices are sent to the address or contact detail designated for that account.

07:05:42.430 --> 07:05:43.250
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:05:43.660 --> 07:05:44.300
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: You

07:05:44.300 --> 07:05:46.300
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: do not send a

07:05:46.300 --> 07:05:50.140
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: separate copy of notices to the account holder spouse, correct?

07:05:50.460 --> 07:05:51.300
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:05:55.100 --> 07:06:01.800
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: And you do not automatically notify the spouse whenever a deposit or a withdrawal is made, correct?

07:06:02.160 --> 07:06:02.900
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:06:03.440 --> 07:06:09.760
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Neither do you automatically inform the spouse of the account's balance at the end of the year, correct?

07:06:10.120 --> 07:06:11.160
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes, sir.

07:06:12.820 --> 07:06:21.460
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: It is the LBP's practice whether the individual account holder is the husband or the wife. It doesn't matter, correct?

07:06:23.170 --> 07:06:29.290
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Kahit yung lalaki or babae, it doesn't matter. Walang difference. Yun yung practice niyo po.

07:06:30.710 --> 07:06:32.250
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The question is [unclear], counsel.

07:06:33.840 --> 07:06:46.200
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: I withdraw your honor. In ordinary banking transactions, the LBP verifies a person's identity and authority before releasing confidential information on the account.

07:06:47.070 --> 07:07:04.790
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Objection, Your Honor. I don't think that the witness is in the position to answer that. She is a branch manager. She is not presented here as a person who is well aware of internal controls at the national level or policy level of land bank, Your Honor. We might endanger the witness with her employment,

07:07:05.030 --> 07:07:05.330
Atty. James Bryan Ibrahim A. Alih: Your Honor.

07:07:05.330 --> 07:07:16.220
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Then she may answer along those lines if she doesn't know. She may answer too if she knows. Objection is overruled. Ma'am Raquel, kung alam niyo po yung sagot, sagutin niyo po. Pag hindi niyo po alam, sabihin niyo rin po.

07:07:18.530 --> 07:07:20.290
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Kindly repeat the question, Attorney CJ.

07:07:21.230 --> 07:07:31.210
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Ma'am, in your practice, LBP verifies a person's identity and authority before releasing confidential account information, correct?

07:07:31.710 --> 07:07:32.330
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes, sir.

07:07:33.380 --> 07:07:42.960
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Your bank would require the depositor or the account holder's written authorization before releasing the account information to a spouse, correct?

07:07:43.820 --> 07:07:47.380
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: We require SPA instead sir, special power of attorney.

07:07:47.380 --> 07:07:47.500
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Oh,

07:07:47.520 --> 07:07:48.920
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: not just a written...

07:07:48.920 --> 07:07:49.720
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Authorization, yes.

07:07:49.720 --> 07:07:50.180
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Thank you.

07:07:50.180 --> 07:07:50.240
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Not just

07:07:50.240 --> 07:07:51.120
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: authorization sir.

07:07:51.320 --> 07:07:59.480
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: So merely naming a spouse in the customer information sheet does not make that spouse a joint account holder, correct?

07:08:00.000 --> 07:08:04.600
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir, unless they're specifically mentioned na mag-or sila or something.

07:08:04.820 --> 07:08:15.090
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Thank you ma'am. A person does not automatically become an authorized signatory merely because he or she is married to that account holder, correct?

07:08:15.630 --> 07:08:16.270
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:08:17.310 --> 07:08:24.510
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Neither does the LBP automatically provide the spouse with access to the account through online banking, correct?

07:08:26.400 --> 07:08:27.820
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Can you repeat the question please?

07:08:28.660 --> 07:08:35.800
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Neither does the LBP automatically provide the spouse with access to the account through online banking, correct?

07:08:36.120 --> 07:08:36.700
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes sir.

07:08:40.560 --> 07:08:48.100
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Thus, marriage alone does not entitle a person to obtain the other spouse's account balance directly from the LVP. Correct?

07:08:48.440 --> 07:08:48.960
Raquel U. Dela Cerna: Yes, sir.

07:08:49.320 --> 07:08:49.880
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: No

